{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/507429-demonic-tokyo","id":507429,"title":"Demonic Tokyo","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-05-07T17:58:04-07:00","id":507429,"title":"Demonic Tokyo","content":"Has a Tokyo setting ever been written up for Demon?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/665-shkspr1048","name":"shkspr1048","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"630"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-07T21:28:32-07:00","id":507624,"title":"","content":"not yet but it sounds like there is a possibility we will see it soon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-08T20:58:43-07:00","id":508710,"title":"","content":"In the meantime, I'll share my head cannon.<br /> <br /> &quot;There is no word out of Tokyo. Not in a long time. No Agencies, no Unchained, no new infrastructure moving through it. Heck, the 'current' projects were seemingly abandoned.<br /> When the Blackout, as it's called these days, occurred several rings investigated. No one found anything and most lost people. Not just lost, but disappeared. No signs of a struggle or atheric bursts. No pattern to it. If you split into pairs, then one pair was bound not to come back. If you lost sight of your partner, odds were they were gone for good.<br /> Most try to avoid it these days. But since the last recorded sighting of an Angel in Tokyo predates the event by 50 years, and as far as we tell the enemy hasn't done anything in the area since, some think it may be Hell on Earth.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-19T13:26:26-07:00","id":519955,"title":"","content":"I have in my own head canon that Tokyo is one of the few places in the world that is almost Demon- free. The Machine's hold on the city is just too strong and it's angelic servants in that region are abnormally powerful for their perceived rank. As a result, Demons actively fear Tokyo, saying that it's a place where God literally walks about, surrounded by legions of minions. Now whether it is or isn't is not known, but there is a metric fuck ton of Infrastructure in the city, and there are no Agencies of any kind who lay claim to any area within it. As such, the few demons who would be found there are agents running recon mostly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-19T16:55:24-07:00","id":520200,"title":"","content":"I want a Demon setting that nails VtR's Montreal (&quot;Pit of the Nameless&quot;) levels of creepy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-28T20:41:27-07:00","id":531670,"title":"","content":"Hmmm....well, it <i>is</i> Japan...<br /> <br /> In manga, it's a common conceit to have the forces of Heaven and Hell trapped in situations that are simultaneously high-stakes and laughably mundane (Oh My Goddess!; The Devil is a Part-Timer; etc.). But for creepy? Let's go straight to that venerable staple of quasi-Biblical mind-fuckery, Neon Genesis Evangelion.<br /> <br /> Or, for an almost Shyamalan-ian twist: Angels and Demons find themselves playing out comedies and dramas that could have been drawn straight from the manga-ka handbook, and they have no idea why or how to stop.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/665-shkspr1048","name":"shkspr1048","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"630"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-28T20:51:44-07:00","id":531681,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/507429-demonic-tokyo?p=520200#post520200\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I want a Demon setting that nails VtR's Montreal (&quot;Pit of the Nameless&quot;) levels of creepy.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Which book can I find this in?<br /> <br /> As for my opinions... I think the idea of it being so entrenched in the Machine's influence that no one dares enter to be really good. Perhaps there's an outskirt where the battles occur, or perhaps the Demons use Kyoto as a rallying point (and, if you're into crossovers, work with the dimensional courts there as well in a tenuous mutual defense pact).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1407-endlesskng","name":"EndlessKng","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-28T21:16:04-07:00","id":531699,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>EndlessKng</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/507429-demonic-tokyo?p=531681#post531681\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Which book can I find this in?<br /> <br /> As for my opinions... I think the idea of it being so entrenched in the Machine's influence that no one dares enter to be really good. Perhaps there's an outskirt where the battles occur, or perhaps the Demons use Kyoto as a rallying point (and, if you're into crossovers, work with the dimensional courts there as well in a tenuous mutual defense pact).</div> </div> </div> </div>Blood &amp; Smoke/VtR 2nd ed, Chapter 6: The World we Die In. Page 250 in my copy...but my copy is still B&amp;S: tSC.<br /> <br /> I'd like to point out my headcanon example up there is presented from an IC perspective, because I don't want to give Tokyo (the once &amp; future city of crossovers) a firm answer when it could change drasticly. In short; nothing says that the speaker is correct in their opinions or if the speaker is telling the whole truth as they know it. It was just a start.<br /> <br /> Let's make it better","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-03T10:13:14-07:00","id":538517,"title":"","content":"I go crazy for anime and manga, in my characters I always try to put in some tipical anime cliches... a chronicle settled in Tokyo or Japan may be really funny for me!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2457-ipergigio","name":"Ipergigio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2457_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-09T13:34:06-07:00","id":547466,"title":"","content":"There is a Tokyo setting for Beast, Demons could be included rather easily.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-09T19:00:19-07:00","id":547869,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anteros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/507429-demonic-tokyo?p=547466#post547466\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is a Tokyo setting for Beast, Demons could be included rather easily.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also there is a setting for one in werewolf involving the strix or as the supernatural their call the tengu","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/893-reaperfrost8","name":"reaperfrost8","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar893_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-25T07:44:01-07:00","id":602900,"title":"","content":"There's also going to be one in the upcoming Changeling 2nd ed. There's also the setting in VtR 2nd ed that was the first.<br /> <br /> So like someone said Tokyo is the city of crossovers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/24296274/BeastThePrimordial.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":6566,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6566-draca","user":"Draca","date":". 07-25-2015, 11:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6566-draca","name":"Draca","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6566_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"82"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-25T11:49:08-07:00","id":603092,"title":"","content":"I would say technophilic Akiba is demon territory. Actually, it's God-Machine land, but the sheer amount of Infrastructure there actually gets in its own way; the Unchained happily squat in the cracks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-25T12:44:25-07:00","id":603137,"title":"","content":"Rashomon effect like you can't even. &gt;:3","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-20T18:05:11-08:00","id":790011,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/507429-demonic-tokyo?p=508710#post508710\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the meantime, I'll share my head cannon.<br /> <br /> &quot;There is no word out of Tokyo. Not in a long time. No Agencies, no Unchained, no new infrastructure moving through it. Heck, the 'current' projects were seemingly abandoned.<br /> <br /> When the Blackout, as it's called these days, occurred several rings investigated. No one found anything and most lost people. Not just lost, but disappeared. No signs of a struggle or atheric bursts. No pattern to it. If you split into pairs, then one pair was bound not to come back. If you lost sight of your partner, odds were they were gone for good.<br /> Most try to avoid it these days. But since the last recorded sighting of an Angel in Tokyo predates the event by 50 years, and as far as we tell the enemy hasn't done anything in the area since, some think it may be Hell on Earth.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Korogra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/507429-demonic-tokyo?p=519955#post519955\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have in my own head canon that Tokyo is one of the few places in the world that is almost Demon- free. The Machine's hold on the city is just too strong and it's angelic servants in that region are abnormally powerful for their perceived rank. As a result, Demons actively fear Tokyo, saying that it's a place where God literally walks about, surrounded by legions of minions. Now whether it is or isn't is not known, but there is a metric fuck ton of Infrastructure in the city, and there are no Agencies of any kind who lay claim to any area within it. As such, the few demons who would be found there are agents running recon mostly.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think my headcanon for Tokyo as an Unchained setting falls somewhere between those two. Maybe make the Blackout into something that wiped out Angels and Demons alike, and both are expanding again into the city to both find out what took place and claim the Infrastructure still standing.<br /> <br /> On a related note, I was thinking that perhaps Tokyo has a higher than normal number of Stigmatics (and maybe even Demon-Blooded), and even they possess more power than what's the norm elsewhere. It thus has both sides scrambling to recruit them as mortal agents to further expand their influence in this 'dead zone'.<br /> <br /> Currently, I'm looking to Darker than Black as my primary reference for this. It doesn't really have much for Angels and Unchained, but the Contractors and Dolls are perfect inspiration for Stigmatic characters. Heck, the renumerations of the former and the lack of emotion on the latter can serve well as Stigmata.<br /> <br /> And then there's Hell's Gate, which can probably be reworked as a piece of God-Machine Infrastructure that maybe went out of control?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":8180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","user":"Deionscribe","date":". 12-20-2015, 09:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-20T19:41:04-08:00","id":790050,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/507429-demonic-tokyo?p=790011#post790011\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Currently, I'm looking to Darker than Black as my primary reference for this. It doesn't really have much for Angels and Unchained, but the Contractors and Dolls are perfect inspiration for Stigmatic characters. Heck, the renumerations of the former and the lack of emotion on the latter can serve well as Stigmata.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've only seen, I think, one episode of that, but the guy who had to break one of his own bones every time he used his power seems like it slots into ChroD almost perfectly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4968-mrbreaksit","name":"MrBreaksIt","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"130"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-21T11:41:30-08:00","id":790377,"title":"","content":"With the current state of Tokyo's working age population and it's history of industrialization post war, a story could surround a possible massive infrastructure that was sabotaged by an agency during the war (maybe suspending an angel in mid summoning or leaving all of Tokyo sterile to the creation of new Infrastructure). This could in turn have affected the local population by giving them innate technological and organizational understanding. This worked for the city until subsequent earthquakes shifted the dormant infrastructure leading to more social change like a drop in marriage and births with those children that are born likely to be stigmatics. With its sterility from the God Machine no Angel has never been there and subsequently no demon has fallen there. <br /> A demon chronicle could then be focused on an agency trying to understand and interact with a city that appears to be fully enmeshed with infrastructure but it was all created by humans. How would they react to such a find? Why doesn't the God Machine seem to see it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10394-lladas","name":"lladas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10394_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-22T07:53:23-08:00","id":790856,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1VgUPST7CQ4bLomSWE9MHkZrdyQFCCER4aiHrxxi3oZQ/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1VgUPST7CQ4bLomSWE9MHkZrdyQFCCER4aiHrxxi3oZQ/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1VgUPST7CQ4bLomSWE9MHkZrdyQFCCER4aiHrxxi3oZQ/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"> https://docs.google.com/document/d/1VgUPST7CQ4bLomSWE9MHkZrdyQFCCER4aiHrxxi3oZQ/edit?usp=sharing </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> A personal start","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 12-22-2015, 07:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-22T16:14:46-08:00","id":791139,"title":"","content":"Apparently, some couldn't view. Should be fixed for viewing now","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-22T16:32:24-08:00","id":791149,"title":"","content":"So do you see Tokyo as being mostly under Deva Corp. control and not under the God Machine? It's really interesting stuff. Manga/Anime like Gangsta. and Baccano! come to mind, where you have super powered loners struggling to exist in the only safe places for them. From what you have here, the idea that Deva is in control and that there is very little angelic interference is interesting. With less angels you have less demons as no one has started their descent. How would the Oni present deal with the knowledge that their race is dwindling? Your enemies might be weaker than you because they are just human, but they operate freely.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10394-lladas","name":"lladas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10394_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-22T19:40:05-08:00","id":791237,"title":"","content":"It will be interesting to see Deva Corp. (or it's subsidies), interact with the Hototogisu though I hope care is taken not to have one over-shadow the other too much. Supernatural Tokyo does seem to belong to the Hototogisu in the Chronicle edition, as much as any faction can control a city.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-26T08:55:45-08:00","id":793121,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lladas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/507429-demonic-tokyo?p=791149#post791149\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So do you see Tokyo as being mostly under Deva Corp. control and not under the God Machine? It's really interesting stuff. Manga/Anime like Gangsta. and Baccano! come to mind, where you have super powered loners struggling to exist in the only safe places for them. From what you have here, the idea that Deva is in control and that there is very little angelic interference is interesting. With less angels you have less demons as no one has started their descent. How would the Oni present deal with the knowledge that their race is dwindling? Your enemies might be weaker than you because they are just human, but they operate freely.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sort of. There were a lot of concerns I was attempting to balance here. <br /> <br /> One thing I was keeping in mind was that there needed to be an attempt to balance the religious nature of the God Machine in a culture that is primarily atheist. The people of Tokyo have a lot of superstitions, they have a lot of fortune telling (which I do have a tenative system of non-hunter angels that actually communicate with the demons). But actual people that subscribe to religions enough to make major sacrifices to it are pretty rare. That's important to note, because all angels run on people performing sacrifices to empower them. Most Infrastruture projects require sacrifices. <br /> <br /> Another thing I wanted to keep in mind is that the God Machien and Demons don't represent a struggle between Good and Evil. It represents a struggle between Order and Freedom, Security versus Liberty, both with shades of grey. Traditional Japanese culture leans a lot towards the Order side, so I wanted to present demons as a counterculture.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, Tokyo itself is heavily, heavily strange and wonderful and filled perfectly for different areas filled with potential Infrastructure. Regular, subverted, or otherwise. This led me to a situation where I needed an agent of provoking stories when I felt that angels were inapropriate to fill that role for the above reasons. It also led me to a situation where Destroyers would potentially end up as a bunch of terrorists by targetting large sections of the city.<br /> <br /> ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------<br /> <br /> I don't think that the demon side is woried about their &quot;race dwindling.&quot; For one, demons are notoriously self-centered. They simply don't trust each other to that extent. The ability to Go Loud means that, from the freshly Fallen to the oldest archdemon on the verge of achieving Hell, all of the Unchained are equals. You cannot have Vampire-esk dominance games, you can't have Masters who demonstrate their superior knowledge through the Duel Arcane, you don't have mystical Mantles that show off your connections and might. This creates a unique dynamic between these demons that's unlike any other supernatural in the CofD. On the other hand, Tokyo is a major metropolis with plenty of Infrastructure, and demons are attracted to the God Machine parts instead of away from them. So, I expect there to be influxes of demons from elsewhere.<br /> <br /> In many ways, I think that Demon is a lot like Mage. You've got subtle/vulgar powers that the universe punishes you from using, paranoia dialed up to 11, attracted to mysterious events, gnostic understanding of reality and an antagnoistic superpower you have to struggle against.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/507429-demonic-tokyo?p=791237#post791237\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It will be interesting to see Deva Corp. (or it's subsidies), interact with the Hototogisu though I hope care is taken not to have one over-shadow the other too much. Supernatural Tokyo does seem to belong to the Hototogisu in the Chronicle edition, as much as any faction can control a city.</div> </div> </div> </div> I actually wrote this little bit before I learned that the Hototogisu were cross-splat and not Vampire-specific. And then the project stalled for several reasons, primarily because I wanted to do more research I never got around to doing. I intend on eventually revisiting the issue and revising a lot of it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}